{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "748fdcc7-6b02-5fdc-8eac-94039edb9124"/*VolumeNoiseExample*/,
  "Description": "Three stages of one chain, left to right. [VolumeNoise] in Displace mode pushes the sphere's surface along fractal noise. [VolumeMorphology] with Dilate grows it outwards, which swells the bumps and closes the dents, and [VolumeFilter] smooths the voxels, which softens what is left.\n\nAKA: displace, noise, blob, organic, smooth, blur, erode, dilate, open, close\n\nTips\n- Smaller VoxelSize means sharper surfaces and more memory and time; start coarse and refine.\n- Level sets store signed distance in world units (negative inside); fog volumes store density.\n- Animated volumes are rebuilt on the CPU every frame; keep their voxels coarse.",
